preConditionHook:
// The trader's equation re-read every bar off the live close: what is left to
// the planned target against what is left to the planned stop. Exit once the
// remaining reward no longer covers a multiple of the remaining risk.
// Both distances are PRICE UNITS from EntryPrice (VERIFIED: contract-weighted
// average, 0.0 when flat, TradeStation does not fold slippage into it).
// The MarketPosition guard is load-bearing rather than decoration: EntryPrice
// reads 0 while flat and a back-adjusted series can carry negative prices, so
// without it both sides would test against a meaningless 0 anchor.
// The parenthesisation matches the EL twin's, so both sides round the same way.
rewardLong = ctx.EntryPrice() + targetPoints - close[0];
riskLong = close[0] - (ctx.EntryPrice() - stopPoints);
rewardShort = close[0] - (ctx.EntryPrice() - targetPoints);
riskShort = ctx.EntryPrice() + stopPoints - close[0];
